      "message": "[error] Line 891: 🔴 `computeExpectedMessages` and its edition/reaction handling rely on `assert(...)` for malformed-history conditions (`commitMap.has_value()`, target lookup in `quickAccess`, mutual exclusivity checks). In DST this turns validation failures into process aborts instead of a controlled test failure, which prevents diagnostic output and can hide which account/commit caused the mismatch. Replace these asserts with explicit runtime checks that log context and return failure (e.g., propagate `false` via `checkMessagesMatch`/`checkAppearances`).",
